# PX4 v1.17 partial QGC overlay for a REAL Quad-X UAV (SYS_HITL=0).
# Aircraft: 3S1P LiPo, 4x SunnySky X2212 980 kV, Holybro PM07 v2.3, Pixhawk 6C, Raspberry Pi 5.
# Candidate slow movement limits only, copied from hardware.params; validated on the 2.0893 kg
# X500 model, NOT on this aircraft. No real flight validation.
# Import only after restoring/checking the real airframe, outputs, sensors and calibrations.
# SYS_AUTOSTART=4001 is generic Quad-X; on an F450-class frame with 10" props, 4011 (DJI F450)
# gives closer starting gains. Verify against the real frame before importing. Reboot after import.
# PM07 voltage/current scaling is NOT set here: keep the Pixhawk 6C defaults, then calibrate
# BAT1_V_DIV / BAT1_A_PER_V in QGC Power setup against a multimeter.
# BAT1_V_EMPTY/CHARGED are standard LiPo per-cell values; check the pack datasheet.
# TELEM2 assumes TX/RX/GND at 921600; unused when the Pi connects by USB as in HARDWARE_SETUP.md.
# HIL outputs and safety-check breakers are cleared explicitly on return from HITL.
# No hover thrust, PID, motor output mapping or offboard-loss action is included.
# This is not a ready-to-fly or complete configuration.
# Vehicle-Id Component-Id Name Value Type
